<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50771" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĕtŭlus</span></b> , a,
		um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj.
				dim.</i> [vetus], <i>little old</i>, <i>old</i> (class.) </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vetulus, decrepitus senex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Merc. 2, 2, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gladiator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Quint. 7, 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">filia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 13, 29, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Lael. 19, 67</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arbor (opp. novella),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fin. 5, 14, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Falernum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					27, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cornix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 13, 25</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cadi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 13, 112, 2</span></i>
			 et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Substt.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĕtŭlus</span></b> ,
				i, m., <i>a little old
				man</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ep. 2, 2, 4</span></i>.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jocularly: mi vetule,</span>”
				<i>my little old fellow</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 7, 16, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĕtŭla</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>a little old
				woman</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 1, 3, 118</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6,
			241</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 8, 79, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
